What are AEC Active Cables?
AEC (Active Electrical Cables) represent a breakthrough in data center connectivity, integrating signal-conditioning components like equalizers or retimers directly into copper cable assemblies. These cables extend the reach of copper beyond passive DAC limitations while maintaining superior power efficiency and cost advantages compared to optical solutions. With global production reaching approximately 1600.9 thousand units in 2025 (averaging $504.5/unit), AEC cables are becoming the go-to solution for short-to-medium reach applications in 400G and 800G data center architectures.
